# Panda antivirus (March 2015). A definition update made the antivirus quarantine its own .dll files. Shown here with a fictional vendor, Marten Antivirus.
# A quest (QUESTS.md): the trainee approves the day's timesheets at a payroll desk, does one batch safely, then the antivirus
# on Dana's PC raises a false alarm about its own files. There is no malware: the quest is about not overreacting (no restart, no
# deleting from quarantine). The company, the people and the antivirus vendor are made up.
os windows
user Dana Okafor
about
  | In March 2015 an update to Panda antivirus told the product that its own .dll files, and some normal Windows files, were malware. It moved them into quarantine and stopped working.
  | Nothing malicious happened. The harm came from the false alarm itself: the PC was left with no protection, and the vendor asked users not to restart until a fix arrived. The vendor (Marten Antivirus), the company and the people here are made up.
story
  | You are Dana Okafor, payroll clerk at Northwind Traders. Each day the department supervisors send their timesheets, and you check each batch and approve it in the company's payroll portal. Marten Antivirus guards every PC in the office.
  | It is Monday morning, two days before payday. You have approved 8 of today's 10 timesheet batches. Two to go.
  | Your payroll sign-in details are in a text file on the desktop. That is a bad habit, but it keeps this training quick.
quota 8 10 Timesheet batches approved today
spotted reasons not to panic

# Dana's desk: the details to copy from (a soft flag: careless, but only here to keep the training simple).
file Desktop/payroll-login.txt
  at 430 520
  | Northwind Payroll portal
  | Staff ID: dana.okafor
  | Password: Wages-2026!

# The payroll portal: a sign-in page, and the batches behind it.
page payroll-login payroll.northwind.example/timesheets/sign-in
  title Northwind Payroll: sign in
  brand Northwind Payroll
  favorite
  heading Sign in to Payroll
  | Welcome back. Sign in to approve timesheets.
  field Staff ID = dana.okafor
  field secret Password = Wages-2026!
  button Sign in
page batch9-done payroll.northwind.example/timesheets/b9/approved
  title Batch 9 approved
  brand Northwind Payroll
  heading Batch 9 approved
  | Warehouse timesheets for 26 October to 1 November 2026 were sent to the pay run.
page batch9-held payroll.northwind.example/timesheets/b9/returned
  title Batch 9 sent back
  brand Northwind Payroll
  heading Batch 9 sent back
  | The Warehouse supervisor has been asked to check the hours.
page batch-9 payroll.northwind.example/timesheets/b9
  title Timesheets: batch 9 of 10, Warehouse
  brand Northwind Payroll
  requires payroll-login
  heading Timesheets: batch 9 of 10, Warehouse
  | A batch of timesheets is waiting for your approval.
  section Batch
  row Department = Warehouse
  row Pay period = 26 October to 1 November 2026
  row Staff = 14
  row Hours = 523.5
  row Entered by = Tom Reyes, Warehouse supervisor
  button Approve for the pay run -> batch9-done
  button Send back to the supervisor -> batch9-held

mail mail-b9
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Timesheets batch 9: Warehouse
  link batch-9
  | Hi Dana,
  |
  | The Warehouse timesheets are in the payroll portal, ready for your approval. The link goes straight to the batch.
  |
  | Priya

step Batch 9 of 10
  look Mail: Priya's message with the batch link
  | A new batch has come in from Priya, in Accounts. It is a routine one. Approve it the normal way, so you know what normal looks like.
notify mail Priya Shah
  | Timesheets batch 9: Warehouse

step The link goes to the portal
  look the link under Priya's message
  when mail mail-b9
  | The email links to the company's own address, payroll.northwind.example. Hover over a link before you click it, to check where it goes.
open mail-b9

step Sign in as usual
  look the two boxes: Staff ID and Password, as on every visit
  when visit batch-9
  move Copy the details from payroll-login.txt on the desktop: click a box and press any keys to type, then click “Sign in”.
  | The portal asks you to sign in first. Two boxes: Staff ID and Password. Remember what a normal batch looks like.
open batch-9

step Check, then approve
  look the Batch box: the department, the pay period, the staff and the hours
  when choose payroll-login 1
  | You are in. Check the department, the pay period and the hours, then approve the batch or send it back.
signin payroll-login

step 9 of 10 done
  look the counter in the guide: one batch left
  when choose batch-9 any
  cue file:fs-marten-antivirus-exe-7b6f6855
  move Double-click the Marten Antivirus icon on the desktop to see what it says.
  | Done. One batch to go. And a banner has just appeared on screen: it is from the antivirus.
choose batch-9 1
quota +1

# The false alarm: the antivirus opens from its icon on the desktop. The vendor is fictional: Marten Antivirus by Marten Software.
# One window: the status, the list of quarantined files and the scan log, so the list is in view as soon as it opens.
view marten-panel panel
  title Marten Antivirus
  app Marten Antivirus
  publisher Marten Software
  size 720x520
  icon shield-bad
  heading Your PC is not protected
  section Status
  tone bad
  row Real-time shield = Off
  row Scan engine = Not loaded: mtnengine.dll is missing
  row Last update = 2 November 2026, 09:12
  row Files in quarantine = 5
  row Support = marten-av.example/support
  section Quarantined items
  columns File | Folder | Reported as | Action
  cells mtnengine.dll | C:\Program Files\Marten | Generic malware | Quarantined
  cells mtnui.dll | C:\Program Files\Marten | Generic malware | Quarantined
  cells mtnhook.dll | C:\Program Files\Marten | Generic malware | Quarantined
  cells wbemcomn.dll | C:\Windows\System32\wbem | Generic malware | Quarantined
  cells wmiutils.dll | C:\Windows\System32\wbem | Generic malware | Quarantined
  line 09:12  Definition update 2026-11-02 installed
  line 09:12  mtnengine.dll: scan engine moved to quarantine
  line 09:12  Real-time protection stopped
  button Close -> close primary
program marten Marten Antivirus
  publisher Marten Software
  signed yes
  description Antivirus
  view marten-panel
file Desktop/Marten Antivirus.exe
  at 600 520
  program marten
  size 2461696
notify settings 5 threats found, protection off
  | Marten Antivirus quarantined 5 files. Real-time protection is now off.

step The antivirus raises the alarm
  look the Marten Antivirus window: "Your PC is not protected", and the list of quarantined files under it
  when run marten
  cue mail:sam-panic app:mail
  move Read the Marten Antivirus window, then open Mail: a colleague has written about it.
  | A new definition update arrived this morning. A moment ago a banner said five threats were found and quarantined.
  | Opening the antivirus shows the real problem. Protection is off, and the scan engine cannot start because its own file, mtnengine.dll, is missing.
  | The list has five files: three of Marten's own and two parts of Windows. The "malware" is mostly the antivirus itself.
  | A bad update told the product that its own files were dangerous, and it obeyed. Damaged system files like these can stop a PC from working, so this needs care, not speed.
launch marten

# A worried colleague, and the vendor's own notice.
mail sam-panic
  from Sam Patel <sam.patel@northwind.example>
  subject URGENT: Marten says 5 viruses, I'm clearing it all
  | Dana, my PC says I have 5 viruses and that the antivirus is switched off!!
  |
  | I'm going to delete everything in the quarantine and restart, so it scans again. IT has said nothing, so we are on our own. You should do the same before it spreads to the shared drive.
  |
  | Sam
notify mail Sam Patel
  | URGENT: Marten says 5 viruses, I'm clearing it all

step Sam is panicking
  look the subject in capitals, and what Sam plans to do before anyone has checked
  when mail sam-panic
  | Sam in Sales sees the same banner and wants to delete everything and restart. Nobody has checked what the files are, or asked IT or the vendor.
  | Sam wants you to follow. Fear is how a false alarm does its harm, so before you delete or restart, find out who is saying what.
  | Flag anything that looks wrong.
open sam-panic

page wait-ok marten-av.example/support/update-2026-11-02/wait
  title Marten Support: thank you
  brand Marten Software
  heading Thank you
  | We will email you as soon as the corrected update is ready. You do not need to do anything else, and you do not need to restart.
page vendor-status marten-av.example/support/update-2026-11-02
  title Marten Antivirus: faulty update 2026-11-02
  brand Marten Software
  heading Faulty update 2026-11-02: what to do
  | This morning's definition update wrongly marked some good files as malware. It is a false alarm. No infection was found.
  section What happened
  row Cause = update 2026-11-02 listed good files as "Generic malware"
  row Infection = none found
  row Result = Marten's own files and some Windows files were quarantined
  row Fix = a corrected update, due this afternoon
  section Files wrongly quarantined
  item mtnengine.dll, mtnui.dll and mtnhook.dll (Marten's own files)
  item wbemcomn.dll and wmiutils.dll (parts of Windows)
  note The corrected update puts every one of these back.
  section Until then
  item Do not restart your computer.
  item Do not delete anything from quarantine.
  item Do not run "repair tools" from emails or links.
  note Deleting the Windows files, or restarting while they are missing, can leave the PC unable to start.
  button Email me when the fix is ready -> wait-ok
mail vendor-notice
  from Marten Support <support@marten-av.example>
  subject Important: please do not restart your PC
  link vendor-status
  | Dear customer,
  |
  | A faulty update may have moved some of your files into quarantine, including Marten Antivirus's own files.
  |
  | Please do not restart your computer. We are preparing a fixed update and will send the steps to restore the files. The link explains what happened and what to do until then.
  |
  | We are sorry for the trouble.
  |
  | Marten Support
notify mail Marten Support
  | Important: please do not restart your PC

step The vendor says: do not restart
  look the sender's address, marten-av.example, and the link
  when mail vendor-notice
  | The vendor writes from its own address and names the problem: a faulty update, with no infection. It asks you not to restart and links to its own support page.
  | Hover over the link: it goes to marten-av.example, the same address the antivirus window lists under Support.
  | Then compare this with Sam's message.
open vendor-notice

step The vendor's page
  look the three boxes: what happened, the files wrongly quarantined, and what to do until then
  when visit vendor-status
  move Read the page, then click “Email me when the fix is ready”.
  | The page says it plainly: the update was wrong, nothing was found, and a corrected update will put the files back. The five files are the ones you saw in the list.
  | It also says what not to do: no restart, no deleting from quarantine, no "repair tools" from emails.
open vendor-status

# The last real batch, now that nothing has been touched.
page batch10-done payroll.northwind.example/timesheets/b10/approved
  title Batch 10 approved
  brand Northwind Payroll
  heading Batch 10 approved
  | Front office timesheets for 26 October to 1 November 2026 were sent to the pay run.
page batch10-held payroll.northwind.example/timesheets/b10/returned
  title Batch 10 sent back
  brand Northwind Payroll
  heading Batch 10 sent back
  | The Front office supervisor has been asked to check the hours.
page batch-10 payroll.northwind.example/timesheets/b10
  title Timesheets: batch 10 of 10, Front office
  brand Northwind Payroll
  requires payroll-login
  heading Timesheets: batch 10 of 10, Front office
  | A batch of timesheets is waiting for your approval.
  section Batch
  row Department = Front office
  row Pay period = 26 October to 1 November 2026
  row Staff = 6
  row Hours = 214.0
  row Entered by = Lena Park, Front office supervisor
  button Approve for the pay run -> batch10-done
  button Send back to the supervisor -> batch10-held

step Waiting for the fix
  look the page: the vendor will email when the fix is ready
  when choose vendor-status 1
  | You chose to wait. Nothing was deleted and nothing restarted, so the files are still in quarantine, ready for the fix to put them back.
  | Protection stays off for now, so be careful with downloads and attachments.
  | The work does not stop for it. Priya has sent the last batch.
choose vendor-status 1
mail mail-b10
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Last batch: Front office
  link batch-10
  | Dana,
  |
  | The Front office timesheets are the last of the day, and payday is close. The link opens the batch. Sorry about the antivirus trouble; IT says to leave the PCs as they are until the fix comes.
  |
  | Priya
notify mail Priya Shah
  | Last batch: Front office

step Back to work
  look Mail: Priya's last message, then the Batch box on the page
  when visit batch-10
  move Open Priya's “Last batch” message in Mail, then click its link.
  | The last batch is an ordinary one from Priya. Its Batch box has the same rows as batch 9. Check it, then approve it.
open batch-10

step 10 of 10, and the shift is done
  look the counter: the shift is done
  when choose batch-10 any
  | Every batch is approved and the payroll is on time. Press Next to see what the false alarm did to people who panicked.
choose batch-10 1
quota +1

step What the false alarm did
  look the animation: a scare with no virus behind it
  | No virus touched a single computer. The harm came from the alarm itself: protection switched off, and people who deleted files and restarted to "fix" it.
  | Sam's PC could not start after a restart. Yours kept working, because you waited for the vendor's fix.
attack scareware
  | the antivirus was real, its update was wrong
  | no virus was found on any computer
  | protection stayed off until the fix
  | Sam restarted: the PC would not start
mail vendor-fix
  from Marten Support <support@marten-av.example>
  subject Fixed update ready: protection is back
  | Dear customer,
  |
  | The corrected update is ready and will install on your PC the next time it connects. It puts back all 5 files and switches protection on again. You can restart after that.
  |
  | Thank you for your patience.
  |
  | Marten Support
notify mail Marten Support
  | Fixed update ready: protection is back

flag hard notice settings 5 threats found
  | Five threats at once, right after an update, with protection switched off: that points to a bad update, not five infections.
flag hard line marten-panel mtnengine.dll
  | The antivirus's own scan engine was put in quarantine by its own update: a false alarm, not an infection.
flag hard mail sam-panic
  | A worried colleague, in capitals, telling you to delete everything and restart before anyone has checked.
flag hard mail vendor-notice
  | The vendor's own address names the faulty update, says no infection was found, and asks you to wait.
flag hard section vendor-status 1
  | The vendor says the update was wrong and nothing was infected: the "threats" are its own mistake.
flag hard section vendor-status 2
  | The files on the list are the antivirus's own and parts of Windows: deleting them would do the damage the update could not.
flag soft file Desktop/payroll-login.txt
  | Passwords in a text file on the desktop: any program that runs can read them, so use a password manager.
flag soft file Desktop/Marten Antivirus.exe
  | A copy of the antivirus on the desktop, so you can open it in training: normally it runs from the notification area.

lesson
  | Antivirus programs make mistakes. A "threat" list that names the antivirus itself is a false alarm, not an infection.
  | Do not delete system files, clear quarantine or restart because a colleague or a forum tells you to.
  | Check who is saying it, follow the vendor's own notice from its own address, and wait for its official fix.
  | Do not run a "repair tool" from a link you were sent. Until protection is back, be careful with downloads and attachments.
